# Kimpor Kang — Construction Portfolio Website

## 1. Project Purpose

Personal single-page portfolio for **Kimpor Kang**, a junior Civil Engineering
student at Paragon International University (Phnom Penh) who works as Project
Coordinator at **Singbuild Construction Co., Ltd.** (design & build contractor,
est. 2015). The site presents real construction / interior fit-out project
experience, skills, side projects, and contact info. Target audience: employers,
clients, and engineering contacts in Phnom Penh and beyond.

## 2. Tech Stack & Constraints

- **Plain HTML5 + CSS3 + vanilla JavaScript** — no frameworks, no bundlers,
  no npm dependencies, no build step.
- Fonts loaded from Google Fonts CDN: `Archivo` (headings), `Inter` (body),
  `IBM Plex Mono` (labels/mono). Site degrades gracefully to system fonts
  offline.
- Deployable as-is on any static host. On Vercel it needs **zero config**
  (no framework, output = repo root, `index.html` entry).
- Do NOT introduce a framework, package.json, or build pipeline unless the
  user explicitly asks — the deliberate simplicity is a design decision.

## 3. File Structure

```
Kimpor-Portfolio-Website/
├── index.html              # The ENTIRE site (single page, ~380 lines)
├── css/
│   └── style.css           # All styling: tokens, layout, responsive (~15 KB)
├── js/
│   └── script.js           # All interactivity (IIFE, strict mode, ES5-safe)
├── images/
│   ├── projects/           # 15 project JPGs referenced by project cards
│   └── _PUT-PHOTOS-HERE.txt# Internal note about photo placement
├── README.md               # Human docs: run, photo map, edit guides
└── kimpor-portfolio.skill  # This file
```

## 4. Design System (css/style.css `:root`)

| Token | Value | Use |
|---|---|---|
| `--ink` / `--ink-2` | `#23262b` / `#3a3f47` | primary text |
| `--slate` | `#5c6570` | secondary text |
| `--paper` | `#f6f4f0` | page background (off-white) |
| `--card` | `#ffffff` | card background |
| `--line` / `--line-dark` | `#e4ded3` / `#3a3f47` | borders |
| `--accent` | `#d97706` | **amber accent** (brand color) |
| `--accent-strong` | `#b45309` | hover shade |
| `--accent-soft` | `#fdf1de` | pale tint backgrounds |
| `--dark` / `--dark-2` | `#1d2024` / `#26292f` | nav/footer dark surfaces |
| `--nav-h` | `66px` | sticky nav height |
| `--radius` | `10px` | card radius |
| `--shadow` | `0 10px 30px rgba(35,38,43,.08)` | card shadow |

Accent alternatives documented in README: steel blue `#2f6f8f/#255a75/#e3eef4`,
safety orange `#e8552d/#c7431f/#fde9e2`. Change all three variables together.

## 5. Page Sections (index.html, in order)

1. **Nav** — sticky dark header, brand mark `KK`, links: About, Projects,
   Skills, Side Projects, Contact (CTA style). Hamburger on mobile.
2. **Hero** — grid-bg, eyebrow "Phnom Penh, Cambodia", name, role, tagline,
   CTA buttons, facts: 15 projects / 11 handed over.
3. **About** (`#about`, label `01`) — bio: Paragon scholarship + Singbuild
   coordination work (reports, BOQ, procurement, RFIs, handover).
4. **Projects** (`#projects`, label `02`) — status filter buttons
   (All / Completed / Ongoing / Upcoming) + grid of 15 `.card` articles,
   each with `data-status` attribute used by the JS filter. Cards show a
   photo from `images/projects/`; missing files fall back to a blueprint-style
   CSS placeholder.
5. **Skills** (`#skills`, label `03`) — two groups: (A) construction
   coordination competencies, (B) software & digital tools (Excel, Apps Script,
   React/Firebase, Vercel, Telegram bots, HTML/CSS/JS).
6. **Side Projects** (`#side-projects`, label `04`) — SB Grab Code Tracker
   (React + Firebase on Vercel) and Manpower Reporting Automation
   (Google Apps Script reading Telegram → Google Sheets).
7. **Contact** (`#contact`, label `05`) — **contains placeholders**:
   `[Add your email]`, `[Add your phone]`, `[Add your LinkedIn URL]` — update
   both visible text and `href` attributes when editing.
8. **Footer** — copyright with JS-injected year, back-to-top link.

Scroll-reveal: elements carry `.reveal` class; JS adds `.is-visible` via
IntersectionObserver (threshold 0.12). Sections use `scroll-margin-top` to
offset the sticky nav.

## 6. JavaScript Behavior (js/script.js)

Single IIFE, `'use strict'`, ES5-compatible (var, function expressions) with
modern APIs guarded:
1. Mobile nav toggle (`#navToggle` / `#navLinks`, `.is-open`, aria-expanded,
   closes on link tap).
2. Scroll reveal via IntersectionObserver; fallback shows everything.
3. Active nav-link highlighting via second IntersectionObserver
   (`rootMargin: -45% 0px -50%`).
4. Project status filter: `.filter-btn[data-filter]` toggles `.is-hidden` on
   `#projectsGrid .card` by matching `data-status`; re-adds `.is-visible` so
   filtered cards don't re-animate.
5. Footer year via `new Date().getFullYear()`.

Keep new JS in the same IIFE style; no external libraries.
